From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Graham Taylor-Jones <graham.taylor-jones@cargt.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:19:32 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: imx91-cargt-00363-00365: tuned RGMII pads

The dts carried the NXP EVK pad values (0x57e data, 0x5fe clocks) for
EQOS and FEC. The iMX93 00365 dts uses the tuned 0x50e (MDC/MDIO) /
0x51e (RGMII) values for the same carrier, so use those on iMX91 too.
On wrynose this took FEC from 339 TX retransmits in a 60 s iperf3 run
to 0.

HS400 and HS400ES are disabled in U-Boot only (U-Boot patch 0040),
because of U-Boot's support for some eMMC parts. HS400 has always
worked in Linux, so Linux keeps it: this patch leaves usdhc1 alone.

Backport of meta-imx-cargt wrynose 0881b68 (!56), by Tim Carney.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Cargt board support]
Signed-off-by: Graham Taylor-Jones <graham.taylor-jones@cargt.com>
---
 .../dts/freescale/imx91-cargt-00363-00365.dts | 56 ++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)

